        "thm-main"
      ],
      "section": "main",
      "statement": "\\label{cor:identity-initialization}\nFix any pair $(c_1,c_2)$ in the range of Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}.  There exist\n$\\widetilde f\\in C^2(\\R^2)$ with a globally H\\\"older continuous Hessian of\nexponent $1/2$, an initial point $\\widetilde x_0\\in\\R^2$, a sequence of positive\nstep lengths $\\{\\alpha_k\\}_{k\\ge0}$, and constants\n$0<\\widetilde m\\le \\widetilde M<\\infty$ with\n$\\widetilde m I\\preceq\\nabla^2\\widetilde f(x)\\preceq\\widetilde M I$\nfor all $x\\in\\R^2$. For this objective function, classical DFP initialized with $\\widetilde H_0=I$ is well\ndefined, and every accepted step satisfies \\eqref{eq:armijo} and\n\\eqref{eq:strong-curvature}.  Nevertheless,\n$\\liminf_{k\\to\\infty}\\|\\nabla\\widetilde f(\\widetilde x_k)\\|>0$.\nThe same conclusion holds in every dimension $n\\ge2$.",
      "statementDependencies": [],
      "title": "The counterexample can start from the identity",
      "type": "Corollary",
      "paperMapping": "Main result in every dimension n ≥ 2.",
      "texLabel": "cor:identity-initialization",
