      "section": "construction",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:disjoint-interpolation}\nThe function $\\Psi$, extended by zero on $\\Gamma$, belongs to\n$C^2(\\R^2)$ and has a globally H\\\"older continuous Hessian with exponent\n$1/2$. It satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interpolation-jets}\n\\Psi(x_k)=0,\\qquad \\nabla\\Psi(x_k)=a_k,\n\\end{equation}\nand\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interpolation-hessian-bound}\n\\sup_{x\\in\\R^2}\\|\\nabla^2\\Psi(x)\\|\n\\le K\\epsilon_0.\n\\end{equation}",
      "statementDependencies": [],
      "title": "Interpolate with a C², one-half Hölder correction",
      "type": "Lemma",
      "paperMapping": "The regularity, interpolation jets, Hölder bound, and Hessian bound are separate declarations.",
